---
import ChartLayout from '../layouts/ChartLayout.astro';
import ChainDiagram from '../components/ChainDiagram.astro';
import { ASSET_OBSERVATION } from '../data/pairSelections';
import { PUBLIC_REPOSITORY } from '../config/site';
---
<ChartLayout title="Robinhood Chain | ONCALL" description="Robinhood Chain, PAR multi-market mechanics and ONCALL evidence boundaries.">
  <p class="meta eyebrow">Case file 04 / Infrastructure record / Handle with gloves</p>
  <h1>Robinhood Chain</h1>
  <p class="lead">One token. Up to five market doors. Still five separate rooms.</p>
  <p class="intro">This file follows the plumbing: network, launcher, quote assets, pools. It does not turn architecture into assurance.</p>

  <section data-public-section aria-labelledby="chain-heading">
    <p class="meta">Official documentation / Accessed 6 September 2026</p>
    <h2 id="chain-heading">The network under the desk</h2>
    <div class="columns"><p>Robinhood describes Robinhood Chain as a permissionless, Ethereum-compatible Layer 2. Its published mainnet settings use chain ID <strong>4663</strong> and ETH for gas. <a href="https://docs.robinhood.com/chain/">Read the chain overview ↗</a></p><p>That description establishes network documentation. It does not establish an ONCALL deployment, a safe contract, a liquid market or permission for a user in any jurisdiction. <a href="https://docs.robinhood.com/chain/connecting/">Inspect network settings ↗</a></p></div>
  </section>

  <section class="mechanics" data-public-section aria-labelledby="mechanics-heading">
    <p class="meta">PAR mechanics / Documentation statement</p>
    <h2 id="mechanics-heading">How a multi-market launch is described</h2>
    <ChainDiagram />
    <div class="columns"><p>PAR says a multi-market launch can open one to five ordinary Uniswap v4 pools for one token in one transaction. Supply is divided equally among the chosen pools while the launch keeps one opening market-capitalization setting across them.</p><p>Each pool is still its own market. A second, third or fifth quote does not create a basket, pooled equity collateral or automatic tracking. Non-ETH quotes must be priceable by PAR’s pricer and meet its in-range depth requirement. <a href="https://par.family/docs">Read PAR documentation ↗</a></p></div>
  </section>

  <aside class="observation" data-public-section aria-labelledby="observation-heading">
    <p class="meta">Dated specimen / Do not read as telemetry</p>
    <h2 id="observation-heading">The observation we can show</h2>
    <p>The official assets API reported the selected LLY, JNJ, HIMS, MRNA and UNH quote deployments as active on chain 4663 at <time datetime={ASSET_OBSERVATION.observedAt}>{ASSET_OBSERVATION.observedAt}</time>. The <a href="/pairs/">Five Pairs file</a> records their exact contracts.</p>
    <p>This dated response does not establish present PAR priceability, route depth, executable liquidity or an ONCALL pool. Those are separate measurements. PAR also states that its contracts are <strong>unaudited</strong>; neither documentation nor a successful transaction proves the absence of contract defects or loss risk.</p>
  </aside>

  <section class="nonclaims" data-public-section aria-labelledby="nonclaims-heading">
    <p class="meta">Before interpreting the structure</p>
    <h2 id="nonclaims-heading">Five things five pairs do not prove</h2>
    <ol><li>ownership of shares in the referenced companies;</li><li>collateral backing for ONCALL;</li><li>index-fund status or issuer endorsement;</li><li>guaranteed price tracking, returns or diversification;</li><li>route quality, liquidity or suitability for any user.</li></ol>
    <p>Stock Tokens are described as tokenized debt securities issued by Robinhood Assets (Jersey) Limited that provide economic exposure without legal or beneficial rights in the underlying issuer. Availability and jurisdiction limits apply. <a href="https://robinhood.com/rhj/stocktokens/">Official Stock Token explanation ↗</a></p>
    <p class="links"><a href="/sources-and-risks/">Open the source and risk ledger</a><a href={PUBLIC_REPOSITORY.href}>Audit the repository ↗</a></p>
  </section>
</ChartLayout>
<style>
  .eyebrow { color: var(--teal); font-weight: 800; }
  h1 { max-width: 12ch; margin-block: .65rem .9rem; font-size: clamp(3.5rem, 8vw, 7rem); letter-spacing: -.045em; overflow-wrap: anywhere; text-transform: uppercase; }
  .lead { max-width: 25ch; color: var(--coral); font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: clamp(1.7rem, 4vw, 3rem); font-weight: 850; line-height: 1; text-transform: uppercase; }
  .intro { max-width: 52ch; margin-top: 1.2rem; font-size: 1.25rem; }
  section, .observation { margin-top: clamp(3rem, 7vw, 6rem); }
  h2 { margin-block: .45rem 1.2rem; font-size: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 3.2rem); text-transform: uppercase; }
  .columns { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: 2rem; }
  .mechanics { padding-block: 1.8rem; border-block: 3px double var(--ink); }
  .mechanics :global(.chain-diagram) { margin-block: 1.5rem 2rem; }
  .observation { padding: clamp(1.25rem, 3vw, 2rem); border: 1px solid var(--ink); border-left: .5rem solid var(--coral); background: var(--paper-raised); box-shadow: .4rem .4rem 0 var(--fur); }
  .observation p + p, .nonclaims p { margin-top: 1rem; }
  .nonclaims ol { margin-block: 1rem 1.5rem; padding-left: 1.5rem; font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: 1.3rem; font-weight: 750; }
  .nonclaims li + li { margin-top: .55rem; }
  .links { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: .6rem 1.5rem; padding-top: 1rem; border-top: 1px solid var(--rule); }
  @media (max-width: 42rem) { .columns { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 1rem; } }
</style>
